==Battleground==
*1 [[Queen B]] spawns as the boss after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Cyberhorn]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
*2 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage forgoes the dense peon spam of the previous stage in exchange for solely tanky enemies, unsupported by small peons. While the enemies here spawn slowly, with around a minute per Cyberhorn/Dark Otter, their high HP pools means that you need to quickly kill them to prevent Queen B from approaching your base and sniping it.

Your main goal should be killing the first Cyberhorn as quickly as possible. Lure the Cyberhorn and Wall Doge to your base, then use anti-Alien CC units as well as high DPS options against Aliens to kill the Cyberhorn.

==='''Key Units'''===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Bahamut is vital to delete Cyberhorn's massive health pool in time, and if not hit by Queen B, Bahamut can reach her and deal massive damage against her before the Dark Otter shows up. Even when it does come, Bahamut alongside your Crazed meatshields and Bombercat can take care of the Dark Otter quickly and allow you to rush down Queen B before the next Cyberhorn appears.
*[[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]: Bombercat moves fast and attacks fast, and can also Freeze Dark Otter. Two desynced Bombercats are able to completely permafreeze Dark Otter, almost completely nullifying its pushing power.
*[[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]]: Even at level 30, Chill's spammability and high DPS against Aliens makes him an excellent option to burst down Cyberhorn. While luring to the base does give you plenty of cash to start off with, Chill costs a lot of money to deploy, so spamming him can quickly leave you broke. If you have access to level 40 units, you most likely won't need Chill, but for a mostly level 30 lineup, Chill is a strong unit to use here.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: While Courier isn't as effective on this stage as the last one, Courier still has excellent mobility and spammability. Courier is best used against the Dark Otter as his LD attacks may miss Cyberhorn, but if positioned well Courier can work against Cyberhorn as well.
*Anti-Alien Crowd Control: Cyberhorn will push very hard if only stalled by meatshields, so you'll want a CC unit to stop it. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] is the best option, as his True Form gains 100% Survive, as well as Freeze just being a better status than Slow, although in a pinch [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] works as well, though be careful of poor RNG.
*[[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]]/[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank]]: Your primary meatshields, as their high speed allows them to get in Queen B's blindspot very easily.

==='''Useful Units'''===
*[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]]: Catellite's poor base health means it'll die quickly to the Dark Otter, but against Cyberhorn, Catellite is able to wall it for good lengths of time.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can's extreme damage shines in this stage, being able to dish out huge damage on both Cyberhorn and Dark Otter, as well as Wall Doge to quickly burst them down. When Talented with its '''Move Speed Up''' and '''Extra Bounties''' Talents, Can Can gets even better as you can farm Extra Money drops on Wall Doge, while also minimizing the odds your Can Can gets Slowed because you mistimed it.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]: Fishman isn't very useful for either Dark Otter or Cyberhorn, but his Massive vs. Floating and high speed allows you to deliver huge chip damage against Queen B if unprotected, allowing you to possibly rush the stage down before the second Cyberhorn or Dark otter appear. Can also be used against Wall Doge.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: One might assume that Pizza is way too slow to actually do anything, but if your rushdown fails and you have to actually fight the Dark Otter, luring alongside Pizza is the fastest way to beat it down. While Pizza may get Slowed, good usage of the Cat Cannon or just sending Pizza and hoping he doesn't get Slowed can allow it to approach Dark Otter and start attacking. If you don't own Bombercat, Pizza is your best unit here to deal with Dark Otter. If you feel that your Pizza isn't dealing enough damage, Talenting Pizza and getting his '''Wave Attack''' Talent increases his average DPS by a lot.
*[[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Saw Cat]]: Power Saw is a stricly better version of Chill for this stage who is used on this stage the same way, but with much better survivability and stats. However, Saw's cooldown is pretty high, so be careful to not let it get too damaged.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Dedicated anti-Dark/Alien Ubers can be used if you find yourself struggling on this stage. Examples include [[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazibastra]], [[Voli (Uber Rare Cat)|Gigavolta]], [[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]], [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]], [[Takeda Shingen (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Shingen]], and [[Mekako Saionji (Uber Rare Cat)|Mission Control Mekako]]. Most of the units you may run here will most likely not be Slow Immune, so try to avoid mistiming your Ubers, or else you'll have spent quite a lot of money for quite a lot of nothing.
*Because all the peons here have poor range, melee Ubers can do well here. Examples include [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]], [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Keiji]], [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]], and [[Iz the Dancer (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz the Alluring Dancer]].
*Most rusher Ubers will be great here given Queen B's presence. Examples include [[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Twinstars Φ]], [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]], [[Count Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Vampiric Yukimura]], [[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]], [[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa χ]], [[Victorious Skanda (Uber Rare Cat)|Zeta Skanda]] [[D'artanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Meow-sketeer]], and [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]].

