'''Battle:''' Instead of luring to your base, this strategy has you lure Cyberhorn to around the halfway mark of the stage. Using Cool Japan and only deploying Seafarer and Can Can to minimize the amount of opportunities Queen B is able to attack and obliterate your stack, you'll eventually get to a position where both Cyberhorn and Dark Otter are near your base. At this position, start spamming Courier while using Bombercat and Awakened Bahamut to Freeze Dark Otter, then get Bahamut to kill Cyberhorn. Once Cyberhorn dies, Bombercat and your attackers will pretty easily kill the Dark Otter. Once it dies, you now have freedom to chip away at most of Queen B's health using your attackers and Butterfly. While the second Cyberhorn will spawn and interupt you, you should have a fat Seafarer stack to completely invalidate its presence, and both Cyberhorn and Queen B should go down pretty easily in the face of your Can Cans and Couriers.

